{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02172",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.17,
      "end_seconds": 7.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.01,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I came as soon as they called me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.08,
      "end_seconds": 11.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.48,
      "end_seconds": 20.95,
      "duration_seconds": 8.47,
      "text": "Okay, so it's pain that comes in waves. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.83,
      "end_seconds": 25.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.5,
      "end_seconds": 43.97,
      "duration_seconds": 16.47,
      "text": "It's been about two weeks, I'm fairly sure. And, And I've been feeling faint as well, uh, for about a month. Yeah, you know, about feeling faint, mostly mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.06,
      "end_seconds": 51.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.76,
      "end_seconds": 63.24,
      "duration_seconds": 10.48,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days. I hardly move around during the day. My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.1,
      "end_seconds": 77.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.53,
      "end_seconds": 83.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Wheat. I come out in... well, itchy skin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.66,
      "end_seconds": 102.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Alright, what do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.3,
      "end_seconds": 110.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "Uh, you know, I'm on iron tablets, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.51,
      "end_seconds": 115.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "I follow. Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.55,
      "end_seconds": 133.56,
      "duration_seconds": 14.01,
      "text": "I have low haemoglobin, for nearly five years. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.01,
      "end_seconds": 146.41,
      "duration_seconds": 11.4,
      "text": "Right, so low haemoglobin is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. And what about discharge, fever or missed period?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.07,
      "end_seconds": 151.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Yeah, no, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.22,
      "end_seconds": 155.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Any sign of vaginal bleeding?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.57,
      "end_seconds": 162.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "No vaginal bleeding, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.14,
      "end_seconds": 168.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.96,
      "end_seconds": 173.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Ah, no, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.13,
      "end_seconds": 178.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.99,
      "end_seconds": 192.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.72,
      "end_seconds": 212.96,
      "duration_seconds": 9.24,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 37.0 degrees, pulse is 115 beats a minute, saturation 98 percent. And blood pressure 133 over 75."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.34,
      "end_seconds": 218.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.42,
      "end_seconds": 222.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.37,
      "end_seconds": 236.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "You are in severe pain with a tender mass low on the right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.6,
      "end_seconds": 242.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.5,
      "end_seconds": 260.58,
      "duration_seconds": 8.08,
      "text": "Putting it all together, this is probably possible ovarian torsion. It could also be appendicitis, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.49,
      "end_seconds": 264.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.14,
      "end_seconds": 279.07,
      "duration_seconds": 12.93,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with possible ovarian torsion do well once it's treated properly. I want an urgent pelvic ultrasound done, that's for possible torsion."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 279.62,
      "end_seconds": 283.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "I can book that for Friday at 9 am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.42,
      "end_seconds": 289.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "You need an emergency scan and probably surgery today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.31,
      "end_seconds": 295.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "Sure. The gynaecology team would be the right next step, I'll refer you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.23,
      "end_seconds": 302.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "Erm, do I need a pregnancy test? I read it might help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.56,
      "end_seconds": 323.42,
      "duration_seconds": 18.86,
      "text": "Okay, I don't think that's needed at this stage, the history doesn't call for it. If the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently. Book a review straight away. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.87,
      "end_seconds": 330.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Right, you know, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}